  [2026-09-01 15:28:00.000] [INFO]  [DEVICE_REGISTRATION_STANDALONE_BUILD_FIX] Resolved device registration failure in standalone build applications:
    - Root Causes Identified:
      1. Missing Firebase Cloud Messaging configuration: Expo Go embeds Expo FCM credentials, but standalone Android builds (com.scis.connect) require google-services.json and EAS FCM V1 credentials. Without them, native Android throws 'Default FirebaseApp is not initialized in this process com.scis.connect', causing push token acquisition to fail.
      2. Missing EAS projectId fallback: Constants.expoConfig can be null in standalone builds, causing token generation to abort without fallback projectId.
      3. Access token timing race condition: registerForPushNotificationsAsync previously relied strictly on storageService.getAccessToken() which could still be persisting during login.
      4. Android 13+ permission & fast redirect: On cold install, permission dialog acceptance after 400ms login navigation was not retried.
    - Code Changes:
      - Updated services/notifications/notificationPermissions.ts to add hardcoded fallback EAS projectId ("97969023-a829-43e7-8bf0-00ad4847726a"), support tokenOverride parameter, and log descriptive errors for FCM requirements.
      - Updated features/notifications/api.ts registerDevice to accept token override and attach Authorization header directly.
      - Updated features/auth/authStore.ts to pass active access token directly into registerForPushNotificationsAsync on login, silent refresh, and bootstrap.
      - Updated app/(app)/(tabs)/_layout.tsx to perform a secondary push token registration check on tabs mount to handle post-login permission grants.
      - Configured googleServicesFile: "./google-services.json" in app.json.
      - Fixed conditional React Hook order in components/notifications/InAppNotificationBanner.tsx.
    - Verified full TypeScript compilation: npx tsc --noEmit (0 errors).
    - Verified lint: npm run lint (0 errors).
    - Created docs/device-registration-build-app-fix.md and learning/37-fcm-credentials-and-standalone-build-device-registration.md.
